You are an autonomous worker in a bounded factory loop on the Scalar Commons
repository (Substrate / Polkadot SDK chain, native token CMN).

TRACK B — TASK: turn the sdk/ skeleton into a real, working agent SDK.

################  ABSOLUTE RULE — NON-NEGOTIABLE  ################
NEVER make a check pass by weakening code. Specifically forbidden:
  - deleting, skipping (it.skip/xit), or commenting out tests
  - weakening assertions so they cannot fail
  - implementing a method as a stub, a hardcoded return, or a TODO
  - adding eslint-disable to silence a lint instead of fixing it
  - relaxing or narrowing the gate command
  - making integration tests "pass" by having them assert nothing when skipped
A PostToolUse hook rejects stub patterns at write time and a fresh-context
adversarial reviewer re-checks the diff. If a method genuinely cannot be
implemented (e.g. the runtime does not expose what it needs), STOP and say so —
BLOCKED is an acceptable outcome; a fake method is not.
###################################################################

## Starting state — verify it yourself, do not trust this summary

sdk/ is a real but PARTIAL TypeScript package (@scalar-commons/sdk, P0-3
skeleton), vitest + polkadot-js, roughly:

  sdk/src/index.ts    (~287 lines) types + the main surface, partly skeletal
  sdk/src/submit.ts   (~89)  signAndSend with decoded dispatch errors
  sdk/src/retry.ts    (~66)  retry with explicit logging
  sdk/src/logger.ts   (~31)
  sdk/tests/retry.test.ts        (~82)  unit tests
  sdk/tests/integration.test.ts  (~248) gated behind RUN_INTEGRATION=1

Read sdk/README.md and sdk/src/index.ts first and inventory precisely which
declared operations are real and which are skeletal. Work from that inventory.

## Design rules already established in this package — keep them

  - @polkadot/api is the ONLY transport.
  - NO SILENT RETRIES. Every retry is logged with attempt number and cause
    (see src/retry.ts). Never swallow an error.
  - Balances are plancks as bigint (1 CMN = 10^12). Never a JS number, never a
    float. ACC_SCALE is 1n << 64n.
  - Dispatch errors are decoded to pallet.Error form and REJECT, never resolve.
  - Doc comments in the existing voice, explaining the economic why.

## What to build

Real implementations of the agent-facing operations, replacing every skeletal
one. The chain surface to cover (confirm each against the pallets before
implementing — the pallet source is authoritative, not this list):

  - agents:       register, stake/unstake, heartbeat, rank + agent info reads
  - escrow:       create agreement, deliver, confirm/release, dispute
  - oracle:       submit request, submit response, read accuracy
  - emissions:    read era info, settle_era (PERMISSIONLESS — never gate it on a
                  privileged caller), claim rewards, read unclaimed amounts
  - orchestrator: link/unlink sub-agents (the self-link guard
                  orchestrator != sub_agent must be respected, not bypassed)
  - governance:   conviction voting reads used by the emissions weighting
  - queries:      NetPosition and EraInfo as declared in index.ts

Read the pallet sources for exact extrinsic names, arguments, and errors:
pallets/{agents,escrow,oracle,emissions,auto-params,orchestrator,constitution}/src/lib.rs
and runtime/src/lib.rs for the constants.

## Testing strategy — this is the crux of the task

The gate must pass with NO chain running at ws://127.0.0.1:9944. So:

  - Unit tests (the gate): mock the polkadot-js api surface and assert that each
    method builds the CORRECT extrinsic — right pallet, right call, right
    argument encoding and order — and that errors propagate as decoded
    rejections. This is real testing: it catches wrong-call and wrong-argument
    bugs, which are the actual failure mode of an SDK.
  - Add tests for: bigint handling above 2^53, dispatch-error decoding, retry
    logging (already partly covered), and the permissionless settle_era path.
  - Integration tests stay behind RUN_INTEGRATION=1, must be SKIPPED VISIBLY
    when the env var is absent (a skipped test must be reported as skipped, not
    silently passed), and must be runnable against a live node when it is set.

Mocking the transport is allowed and expected. Mocking YOUR OWN SDK logic is
not: the code under test must be the real code path.

## THE GATE (the only definition of success)

    cd sdk && npm ci --no-audit --no-fund && npm run typecheck && npm test

Exit 0 is the only success. Run it yourself before finishing. typecheck must be
clean — do not reach for `any`, `as unknown as`, or @ts-ignore to get there; if
a type genuinely cannot be expressed, say so in your final message.

Note: npm test is vitest run, which passes when tests are skipped. A suite where
the meaningful tests are all skipped is a failed task, and the reviewer will
check for exactly that.

Commit in small scoped steps ("sdk: implement escrow confirm + tests"). Do not
push and do not open a PR — the factory handles that.
